From: SC130 platform maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: uvc: allow framebased queue capacity configuration

Framebased descriptors intentionally omit dwMaxVideoFrameBufferSize, but the
gadget V4L2 queue still uses the internal value as sizeimage. Expose the existing
attribute for framebased frames so userspace can configure a bounded maximum
access unit instead of inheriting the 460800-byte default for a 640x360 frame.
This attribute affects queue allocation only, not the framebased USB descriptor.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_configfs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_configfs.c
@@ -2137,6 +2137,7 @@ static struct configfs_attribute *uvcg_frame_attrs2[] = {
 	&uvcg_frame_attr_dw_max_bit_rate,
 	&uvcg_frame_attr_dw_default_frame_interval,
 	&uvcg_frame_attr_dw_frame_interval,
+	&uvcg_frame_attr_dw_max_video_frame_buffer_size,
 	&uvcg_frame_attr_dw_bytes_perline,
 	NULL,
 };
